The edit was successful with no linter errors."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"

I've created a proper inheritance hierarchy following the Single Responsibility Principle:

1. Created a `BaseAlarmFeedbackPlayer` abstract class that defines common behavior
2. Modified `VibrationPlayerImpl` and `RingPlayerImpl` to extend the base class
3. Created a new `CombinedAlarmPlayerImpl` that:
 - Extends BaseAlarmFeedbackPlayer
 - Implements AlarmFeedbackPlayer interface
 - Delegates to RingPlayer and VibrationPlayer for specific functionality

This approach:
- Follows the Single Responsibility Principle by keeping specific functionality in respective classes
- Uses inheritance appropriately with the base class providing common structure
- Implements composition in the CombinedAlarmPlayerImpl for more flexibility
- Provides a clean interface for alarm feedback

The combined player can be used when you need both sound and vibration, while the individual players can be used separately when only one type of feedback is needed."}]}]}
